---
name: Infrastructure Rules
globs: src/Core/**/*.Infrastructure/**, src/Shared/Kernel.Infrastructure/**
alwaysApply: false
---

## Entity Framework Core

- Single `AppDbContext` in `Kernel.Infrastructure/Persistence/`.
- One configuration class per entity: `{Entity}Configurations : IEntityTypeConfiguration<{Entity}>` in `Kernel.Infrastructure/Persistence/Configurations/`.
- Table name = plural of entity (`Users`, `Roles`). Always set `HasKey`, `ValueGeneratedNever()` for `Id`.
- Value objects mapped with `OwnsOne()`. Relationships use explicit FK and `OnDelete`.

### Interceptors

| Interceptor | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|
| `AuditableEntityInterceptor` | Auto-fills `CreatedBy/At`, `UpdatedBy/At` on SaveChanges. |
| `MultiTenantSaveChangesInterceptor` | Sets `TenantId` on new `IMultiTenantEntity` entries. |
| `SearchPathConnectionInterceptor` | Sets PostgreSQL `search_path` for schema-per-tenant. |

### Seeders

Located in `{Module}.Infrastructure/Data/Seeders/`. Pattern: `{Entity}Seeder.SeedAsync(context)`. Always idempotent — check `AnyAsync()` before inserting.

> For migration creation and EF workflow → invoke `/new-migration`.

## Repositories

- Interface: `I{AggregateRoot}Repository : IBaseRepository<T>` in Domain.
- Implementation: `{AggregateRoot}Repository` in `{Module}.Infrastructure/Data/Persistence/`.
- Eager loading via `Include`/`ThenInclude` for aggregate children.
- **Never return `IQueryable<T>`** from a repository.

> For complex read query optimization → invoke `/optimize-query`.

## Unit of Work

```csharp
await _repository.AddAsync(entity, cancellationToken);
await _unitOfWork.Commit(cancellationToken);
```

Only command handlers call `Commit()`. Query handlers never commit.

## Multi-Tenancy Infrastructure

`TenantResolutionMiddleware` → `CachedTenantStore` → `TenantContext` (scoped per request).
`ModelBuilderTenantExtensions` applies `HasQueryFilter` for `TenantId` on all `IMultiTenantEntity`.

## DI Registration

Register in `{Module}.Infrastructure/DependencyInjection.cs`, wire via `CoreConfiguration.cs`:

```csharp
services.AddScoped<I{Entity}Repository, {Entity}Repository>();
```

## External Integrations

Use `IHttpClientFactory` with resilience policies from `ResilienceConfiguration`. Never call external APIs from Domain or Application — wrap in an infrastructure service behind an interface.
